{
  "summary": "Applies two upstream backport patches to Cap'n Proto in depends to fix non-atomic reads in debug assertions. It replaces raw memory reads of mutex futex states and atomic reference counters with relaxed atomic loads.",
  "problem": "Unoptimized builds, including ThreadSanitizer (TSan) CI jobs, enable Cap'n Proto debug assertions that inspect mutex futex words and atomic reference counts non-atomically. When objects communicate across threads, TSan flags these debug reads as data races, failing CI runs.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'The TSan job builds capnp without optimization, which automatically enables these assertions, and TSan reports these reads as data races the moment KJ objects start communicating across threads.'",
    "Links to a concrete CI failure in bitcoin-core/libmultiprocess#376 triggered by switching EventLoop::sync() to kj::Executor::executeSync().",
    "Patches correspond directly to upstream Cap'n Proto backport commits b91a6ba7c7 and cc13c8c45f (capnproto/capnproto#2855)."
  ],
